\hypertarget{variable-names-labels-and-descriptions}{%
\subsection{Variable names, labels and
descriptions}\label{variable-names-labels-and-descriptions}}

The name and label for each independent variable are presented in ,
along with the group that compiled each variable and the constraint that
was applied to each variable to mitigate the potential for outliers to
have an outsized influence on the results. For example, 0.50 for
Book-to-market equity means the variable was constrained at
0.5\textsuperscript{th} percentile and the 99.5\textsuperscript{th}
percentile. A description for each variable is in the appendix. Each
group has compiled a paragraph explaining how the variable is computed,
the source of the data and why there is a plausible reason this
characteristic is associated with industry-adjusted returns.

